; TEST: expect-exit=100 c-emit-exit=4
;
; The op words beyond `fadd`/`add`: `mul` (whose identity is 1, not 0) and
; the wrapping and saturating pair, in both shapes. Each fold and each tree
; combine is the STANDALONE opcode -- emit.inc routes them through
; __bfa_emit_mul_core and __bfa_emit_sat_core, the same routines the
; dispatcher's `mul`/`adds` reach -- so the overflow behaviour of a reduction
; is the overflow behaviour of its operator, with nothing extra and nothing
; lost (ssa-ir.md 2.6, as defined 2026-09-25).
;
;   1  mul  i64, ordinata,  [2, 3, 7]        = 42    (1*2*3*7; identity 1)
;   2  mul  i64, arborea 4, [2, 3, 7, 1]     = 42    ((2*3)*(7*1)) folded
;                                                     into acc = 1
;   3  addw u8,  ordinata,  [200, 100]       = 44    300 mod 256 -- WRAPS,
;                                                     does not trap
;   4  adds u8,  ordinata,  [200, 100]       = 255   saturates at the top
;   5  subs u8,  ordinata,  [200]            = 0     0 -| 200 clamps at 0,
;                                                     the identity-first fold
;   6  addw u8,  arborea 2, [200, 100]       = 44    the WRAP happens inside
;                                                     the group tree
;
; CHECK 2 is the same product by a different tree: integer multiplication is
; associative, so the value cannot distinguish the shapes -- what it checks
; is that the tree is built and folded at all, and that `mul`'s identity
; seeds the accumulator (a 0 would make it 0). The shapes are distinguished
; where it is observable, over floats: red_arborea_f32.ir.
;
; CHECK 5 is `subs` read off the definition: acc starts at the identity 0 and
; every contribution folds, so one contribution of 200 gives 0 -| 200, which
; a saturating unsigned subtract clamps to 0 rather than wrapping to 56.
;
; CHECK 6 puts a wrapping op inside a group, where a trapping one would
; abort (red_arborea_int_trap.ir): the tree combine is `addw`, so 200 + 100
; is 44 in the cell and the fold adds it to an accumulator of 0.
;
; Mutation (run): `mul`'s identity taken as 0 -> exit 1 and 2. `adds`/`subs`
; folded without their clamp -> exit 4 (300 normalised to 44) and exit 5
; (0 - 200 wrapped to 56). The tree combine using a trapping `add` where the
; op word says `addw` -> check 6 aborts instead of returning 100.
;
; `c-emit-exit=4`: the C backend refuses the reduction opcodes by name
; (c-backend.md D4 rows 36-38).

functio @initium (ptr) -> u8 {
b0:
%0 = param ptr 0
%1 = iconst i64 2
%2 = iconst i64 3
%3 = iconst i64 7
%4 = iconst i64 1
%5 = redinit i64 mul ordinata 0
contrib %5 %1
contrib %5 %2
contrib %5 %3
%6 = redfin i64 %5
%7 = iconst i64 42
%8 = cmp.eq i64 %6 %7
br %8 b2 b1
b1:
%9 = iconst u8 1
ret %9
b2:
%10 = redinit i64 mul arborea 4
contrib %10 %1
contrib %10 %2
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %4
%11 = redfin i64 %10
%12 = cmp.eq i64 %11 %7
br %12 b4 b3
b3:
%13 = iconst u8 2
ret %13
b4:
%14 = iconst u8 200
%15 = iconst u8 100
%16 = redinit u8 addw ordinata 0
contrib %16 %14
contrib %16 %15
%17 = redfin u8 %16
%18 = iconst u8 44
%19 = cmp.eq u8 %17 %18
br %19 b6 b5
b5:
%20 = iconst u8 3
ret %20
b6:
%21 = redinit u8 adds ordinata 0
contrib %21 %14
contrib %21 %15
%22 = redfin u8 %21
%23 = iconst u8 255
%24 = cmp.eq u8 %22 %23
br %24 b8 b7
b7:
%25 = iconst u8 4
ret %25
b8:
%26 = redinit u8 subs ordinata 0
contrib %26 %14
%27 = redfin u8 %26
%28 = iconst u8 0
%29 = cmp.eq u8 %27 %28
br %29 b10 b9
b9:
%30 = iconst u8 5
ret %30
b10:
%31 = redinit u8 addw arborea 2
contrib %31 %14
contrib %31 %15
%32 = redfin u8 %31
%33 = cmp.eq u8 %32 %18
br %33 b12 b11
b11:
%34 = iconst u8 6
ret %34
b12:
%35 = iconst u8 100
ret %35
}
